WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:07.330
You didn't start my timer.

00:00:07.330 --> 00:00:11.330
President Obama: We're in the middle of the
longest streak of private sector job creation

00:00:11.330 --> 00:00:13.240
in history.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:23.640
More than 14 million new jobs, the strongest
2 years of job growth since the 1990s, an

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:25.689
unemployment rate cut in half.

00:00:25.689 --> 00:00:30.670
Michael: In his final State of the Union address,
President Obama touted the fact that the unemployment

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.509
rate has been cut in half.

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:35.610
The President is right to celebrate the unemployment
rate.

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:40.749
Its fall represents the alleviation of hardship
for millions of American workers.

00:00:40.749 --> 00:00:45.870
Unfortunately the job market has much further
to go before all Americans who can be working

00:00:45.870 --> 00:00:50.929
and who should be working are in jobs that
they're satisfied with.

00:00:50.929 --> 00:00:53.879
And unfortunately, several of the policies
the President has championed throughout the

00:00:53.879 --> 00:00:58.660
course of his administration have made it
harder to find a job, not easier.

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:00.239
Let's take two.

00:01:00.239 --> 00:01:01.629
One is the minimum wage.

00:01:01.629 --> 00:01:05.320
The President is wrong to insist on a higher
minimum wage.

00:01:05.320 --> 00:01:08.040
Raising the minimum wage makes it harder for
people to work.

00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:12.829
Instead, the President should be touting wage
subsidies that pull people into the work force

00:01:12.829 --> 00:01:14.030
and that encourage work.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:18.360
In addition, the Affordable Care Act should
be repealed and replaced in a responsible

00:01:18.360 --> 00:01:23.640
manner that makes it possible for Americans
who want health insurance to get it, but that

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:26.590
doesn't erect barriers to employment.

00:01:26.590 --> 00:01:29.659
So what do you think of President Obama's
legacy?

00:01:29.659 --> 00:01:33.360
Let us know if there are any other topics
you would like to see AEI scholars discuss

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:34.439
in 60 seconds.

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:38.740
And be sure to check out other State of the
Union responses from my AEI colleagues.

